# A built-in function that is passed to a function that calls it is a known callee, as a function of the program is: `each(Boolean, x)`. All who pass one built-in function call one copy,
# also where the call is seldom run, and in the copy the parameter holds that built-in and nothing else. A built-in object that is no function gets none
# FORM: Prepared
# RUN: pass InlineCalls
# STATISTIC: CalleeVersions = 2
# CHECK: outcome: Changed

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f3
entry module=m0
function f0 name="each" parameters=[{type=anything}, {type=anything}, {type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: anything, v1: anything, v2: anything):
    v3 = TypeTest v0 testedType=function
    Branch v3 -> taken b1(| 0), notTaken b2()
  b1(v4: function):
    v5 = Integer integer=0
    v6 = Call v4, v2, v1, v5, v1
    v7 = Add v6, v1
